            <ArticleTitle>Enigmatic pain referred to the teeth and jaws.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>182-6; quiz 187-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A number of obscure syndromes can mimic dental or jaw pain in the absence of pathosis within these structures. This enigmatic dental pain includes conditions such as pretrigeminal neuralgia, complex regional pain syndrome, temporal tendinitis, and carotodynia. Each of these syndromes is described through a pertinent case report to illustrate appropriate diagnosis and treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
